= BITwiki organization =

BITwiki is organized so knowledge can be read as coherent pages, queried as semantic data, navigated as a graph, and reused as modular content.

== MediaWiki primitives first ==
; Page
: durable knowledge object or documentation unit.
; Namespace
: broad system/page-class boundary with distinct MediaWiki behavior.
; Category
: human-readable grouping and navigation mechanism.
; Template
: reusable transcluded content or interface.
; Property
: Semantic MediaWiki attribute or relation.
; Concept
: stored semantic query / computed collection where appropriate.
; Module
: reusable executable wiki logic where templates are insufficient.
; Redirect
: title continuity and migration mechanism.
; Revision / history / diff
: provenance and correction trail.

== Independent dimensions ==
<pre>
namespace ≠ entity type ≠ domain ≠ Book Matter ≠ epistemic status ≠ relationship
</pre>

== Entity type ==
Entity type answers: '''what kind of thing is this knowledge object about?''' V1 contains multiple entity/page-type vocabularies that remain to be reconciled. Do not invent a final controlled vocabulary until those source pages have been compared.

== Domain ==
Domain answers: '''what field or body of knowledge does this belong to?''' Systems science is a foundational orientation. Historical portal priorities also include Science, Biology, Mathematics, Philosophy, Technology, Electronics, Energy, Engineering, Chemistry, Physics, and Medicine.

== Relationships ==
Semantic relationships express how knowledge objects connect. Relationship vocabulary should be recovered from [[BITwiki Relationship Types]], [[BITwiki Relationship Pattern Catalog]], and actual content before being finalized.

== Navigation as a view ==
Portals, indices, outlines, contents pages, category trees, semantic queries, and knowledge graphs are views over the underlying knowledge model. Navigation should help a reader traverse the map; it should not become the ontology merely because it is visible.

